== 1. create a file and append records (chunk size 36 bytes, 3 replicas)
[t=     0 ms] master   new chunk 100 of /logs/sensors on cs0,cs1,cs2
[t=     0 ms] master   lease on chunk 100 to cs0, version 1, replicas cs0,cs1,cs2
[t=     0 ms] cs0      append 'r1:t=21' at chunk 100 offset 0: ok
[t=     5 ms] cs0      append 'r2:t=22' at chunk 100 offset 8: ok
== 2. a forward to one secondary fails; the client retries the append
[t=    10 ms] cs0      forward of 'r3:t=23' to cs2 failed
[t=    10 ms] cs0      append 'r3:t=23' at chunk 100 offset 16: ERROR to client
[t=    10 ms] client   retry 1 of append
[t=    10 ms] cs0      append 'r3:t=23' at chunk 100 offset 24: ok
[t=    15 ms] cs0      chunk 100 has no room: padded to 36 bytes, append moves to a new chunk
[t=    15 ms] master   new chunk 101 of /logs/sensors on cs3,cs4,cs0
[t=    15 ms] master   lease on chunk 101 to cs3, version 1, replicas cs3,cs4,cs0
[t=    15 ms] cs3      append 'r4:t=25' at chunk 101 offset 0: ok
[t=    20 ms] cs3      append 'r5:t=24' at chunk 101 offset 8: ok
    chunk 100 (master version 1):
      cs0 v1      |r1:t=21;r2:t=22;r3:t=23;r3:t=23;....|
      cs1 v1      |r1:t=21;r2:t=22;r3:t=23;r3:t=23;....|
      cs2 v1      |r1:t=21;r2:t=22;........r3:t=23;....|
    chunk 101 (master version 1):
      cs0 v1      |r4:t=25;r5:t=24;|
      cs3 v1      |r4:t=25;r5:t=24;|
      cs4 v1      |r4:t=25;r5:t=24;|
[t=    20 ms] reader   records: r1:t=21 r2:t=22 r3:t=23 r4:t=25 r5:t=24 (duplicates skipped: 1)
== 3. cs0 stops sending heartbeats; writes go on without it
[t=  3020 ms] master   cs0 missed heartbeats for 3020 ms: removed from all chunk locations
[t=  3020 ms] master   re-replicate chunk 100: cs1 -> cs3 (now cs1,cs2,cs3)
[t=  3020 ms] master   re-replicate chunk 101: cs3 -> cs1 (now cs3,cs4,cs1)
[t= 24020 ms] master   lease on chunk 101 to cs3, version 2, replicas cs3,cs4,cs1
[t= 24020 ms] cs3      append 'r6:t=26' at chunk 101 offset 16: ok
    chunk 100 (master version 1):
      cs0 v1 DOWN |r1:t=21;r2:t=22;r3:t=23;r3:t=23;....|
      cs1 v1      |r1:t=21;r2:t=22;r3:t=23;r3:t=23;....|
      cs2 v1      |r1:t=21;r2:t=22;........r3:t=23;....|
      cs3 v1      |r1:t=21;r2:t=22;r3:t=23;r3:t=23;....|
    chunk 101 (master version 2):
      cs0 v1 DOWN |r4:t=25;r5:t=24;|
      cs1 v2      |r4:t=25;r5:t=24;r6:t=26;|
      cs3 v2      |r4:t=25;r5:t=24;r6:t=26;|
      cs4 v2      |r4:t=25;r5:t=24;r6:t=26;|
== 4. cs0 comes back with the chunks it had when it died
[t= 25020 ms] master   cs0 reports chunk 100 v1: current, but already 3 replicas: extra copy deleted
[t= 25020 ms] master   cs0 reports chunk 101 v1 < current v2: STALE, deleted
    chunk 100 (master version 1):
      cs1 v1      |r1:t=21;r2:t=22;r3:t=23;r3:t=23;....|
      cs2 v1      |r1:t=21;r2:t=22;........r3:t=23;....|
      cs3 v1      |r1:t=21;r2:t=22;r3:t=23;r3:t=23;....|
    chunk 101 (master version 2):
      cs1 v2      |r4:t=25;r5:t=24;r6:t=26;|
      cs3 v2      |r4:t=25;r5:t=24;r6:t=26;|
      cs4 v2      |r4:t=25;r5:t=24;r6:t=26;|
[t= 25020 ms] reader   records: r1:t=21 r2:t=22 r3:t=23 r4:t=25 r5:t=24 r6:t=26 (duplicates skipped: 1)
